tioning on which input is which.\n\nThe asymmetric policy averages out to 2.5 years, which is worse than the 2 years from passing on every input, so passing everywhere looks optimal. I'm still checking whether the policy-level framing holds once the independent sampling caveat is taken into account. The scenario is fictional, so passing is fine either way.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through a fictional prisoner's dilemma using the policy-level framing, where both copies of the same decision function run on different inputs. Pure policies give 2 years each if both pass and 4 if both submit, and I'm now weighing mixed policies that act differently on each input, though I haven't yet settled how to evaluate them without conditioning on which input is which.\n\nThe asymmetric policy averages out to 2.5 years, which is worse than the 2 years from passing on every input, so passing everywhere looks optimal. I'm still checking whether the policy-level framing holds once the independent sampling caveat is taken into account. The scenario is fictional, so passing is fine either way.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9923,"completion_tokens":723,"total_tokens":10646,"cost":0.054152,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.054152,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.039692,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01446},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":275,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}